# Netlify rewrites — keep URL clean while routing to the entry HTML.
# 200 = internal rewrite (URL bar unchanged); a 301/302 would visibly redirect.

# Deep-link "take" URLs: /take/cefr-reading-45  →  /landing-v3.html?take=cefr-reading-45
# Shared in Telegram channels so followers land directly on the access-code
# modal for that specific mock instead of navigating through the welcome
# page + skill picker + scroll-to-mock flow.
#
# As of 2026-05-21: target flipped from landing.html to landing-v3.html.
# v3 has its own _processDeepLinkTakeV3 (commit 6809b1b) that runs through
# the inline pickers + handle*MockClick handlers. Avoids landing.html's
# loadMock iframe path which had a return-to-v3 quirk that bounced users
# back to /landing-v3.html instead of opening the speaking mock on first
# code submit.
/take/* /landing-v3.html?take=:splat 200

# VIP deep link: /vip/<code> → the Profile tab with the code box focused and
# the code already typed in. Students were being told "open the menu, find the
# VIP field, type this" — three steps that some never completed. A teacher can
# now send one link. Bare /vip works too: it opens the box, empty.
/vip /landing-v3.html?vip=1 200
/vip/* /landing-v3.html?vip=:splat 200

# landing-v2.html was an abandoned design iteration (deleted 2026-07-20).
# 301 any stray old bookmark to the live landing.
/landing-v2.html /landing-v3.html 301

# Desktop app download shortlinks. These lived only in netlify.toml, which
# Cloudflare Pages does not read — so they move here, where both hosts see
# them. 302 (not 200) because the target is an external host: Pages can only
# proxy relative URLs, and a redirect keeps the student's link working if we
# re-point the target later.
/desktop    https://storage.googleapis.com/mockstream-desktop-releases/download.html   302
/download   https://storage.googleapis.com/mockstream-desktop-releases/download.html   302
